"""Level Factory 0.273.0: the draw distance on the export's merged meshes, and a solid object's silhouette kept.

`merge_buildings.gd` and `merge_empties.gd` give each merged mesh they make (`MergedR_*`, `Merged<side>_*`) the
distance at which it spans 3 px of a 1080-line screen through the game's camera -- the rule `zoo_worldskin.gd` gave
an object's parts in 0.272.0, its constants held equal across the three scripts -- and keep a lit one, a lit face's
mesh and a pane to every distance; the Python halves refuse a report that does not account for every merged mesh.
At import, an object carrying a collider keeps its largest part at every distance (the walker's draw-distance
handoff, REQ-001 and VAL-004: cover stays visible wherever it can stop a shot), and `DRAW_ZOOM` multiplies every range
for a game that adds a scope.

Proven: tests/unit/test_merged_draw_distance.py and tests/unit/test_merge_buildings_godot.py (a real Godot merge)
fail on 0.272.0 (fails_on_old.out.txt); the clone's suite (suite_clone.out.txt); the slice rebuilt and priced against
slice 20 (the factory's docs/findings/slice_look/, slice 21).
"""
